-- title:
--   Level automorphisms attached to Γ(q)∩Γ₀(M') number #SL₂(ℤ/ℓ')
-- statement:
--   Let $q \ge 5$ and $\ell' \ge 3$ be primes with $\ell' \neq q$, and let $M' \ge 1$ be divisible by neither $q$ nor $\ell'$. A package of reduction data at $q$ is assumed, summarised here: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit; a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places for $q$ (rational places that are affine geometric places at which the value of $\mathrm{jGeomGen}$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$), together with a chosen element $s$ of $W$; the containment $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of subfields of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$, the former generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ and the latter by those of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the units of $\mathbb Z/q^2M'$ congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$, i.e. a valuation subring of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal and compatible with the residue map of $A$, and a degree-preserving map on places compatible with order functions; and the hypothesis $hR_0$ that for a Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Further, let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$ such that $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field, and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$; let $\xi \in k_0$ be a primitive $q\ell'$-th root of unity. Finally let $K_\ell$ be the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $X_H$ function field of level $N_0 = (q\ell')^2M'$ with $H = \mathrm{levelH}(q\ell', M')$ the group of units of $\mathbb Z/N_0$ congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$, with $A_0$-algebra and scalar-tower structures on it, and let $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $j_q$ of the modular invariant. Then the number of $k_0$-algebra automorphisms $\tau$ of $K_\ell$ for which there exists $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ with $\tau$ the level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$, in the sense that for every weight $k$, every pair $f, g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ and with the rational series attached to $p_g$ nonzero, every $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the quotient of the rational series of $p_f$ by that of $p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, one has that the coefficientwise $\iota$-image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \delta$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \delta$, where $\delta$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b/m \\ mc & d\end{pmatrix}$ built from $\gamma^{-1} = \begin{pmatrix} a& b\\ c& d\end{pmatrix}$ with $m = q\ell'$, equals $\#\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z/\ell')$.
--
--   This is the counting step for the auxiliary level $q\ell'$ introduced over the field of constants $k_0$: the assignment $\gamma \mapsto \tau_{\gamma^{-1}}$ on $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ has image of the same size as $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z/\ell')$, reduction modulo $\ell'$ being surjective on $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ with the same kernel as $\gamma \mapsto \tau_{\gamma^{-1}}$. It feeds the orbit–stabiliser computation in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_levelAut_stabilizer_eq_natCard_rationalAut_of_moduliPlace`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_levelAut_stabilizer_eq_natCard_rationalAut_of_moduliPlace).
